# <%= current_page.data.title %>

We are in discovery to understand how teams across the Ministry of Justice monitor and investigate the behaviour of their applications and infrastructure.

This work will help us understand what a future Observability Platform should provide, based on teams' needs and experiences rather than starting with a selected tool.

## Current service and future discovery

The existing Observability Platform is hosted on Modernisation Platform and uses Amazon Managed Grafana. Its [architecture](/architecture/) and [runbooks](/runbooks/) describe the current service.

The current offering is intended to be retired in the future. This discovery does not announce a retirement date or migration timetable, and does not mean the current service has closed. Existing onboarding and access guidance remains in the [user guide](https://user-guide.observability-platform.service.justice.gov.uk/).

The discovery has a broader scope than the existing service. We want to understand experiences across Modernisation Platform, Cloud Platform, and other Ministry of Justice teams. Taking part does not mean a team is onboarding to a new service.

## What discovery is for

We want to understand:

- The observability tools and approaches teams use today.
- What works well and where there are gaps or difficulties.
- How teams monitor service health and investigate incidents.
- The effort involved in operating and maintaining existing tooling.
- Shared requirements and differences between teams and environments.

Read more about [understanding teams' needs](/discovery/understanding-team-needs.html) and the [capabilities being explored](/discovery/offerings.html).

## What remains undecided

The future solution, architecture, and service offering have not been established through this discovery. The topics documented here are areas to investigate, not a committed service catalogue or delivery roadmap.

These pages do not announce a selected supplier, a replacement service ready for use, or a migration requirement for existing users.

## Contribute to discovery

Tell us about your team's current setup, what works, and what you would like to improve through [#ask-observability-platform](https://moj.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C05QXHR697S).

You do not need to have a proposed solution to contribute. Please do not post credentials, sensitive telemetry, or restricted architecture details in public documentation; ask the team how to share sensitive information appropriately.
